  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Sniffer Dogs and the Detection of Illegal Pangolin Trade in the Republic of Congo</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The purpose of this project is to support a sniffer dog program to combat the illegal trade in pangolin scales and bushmeat in the Republic of Congo. This project is intended to conserve pangolins and other trafficked species by disrupting illegal trade. Specific activities include: (1) daily field missions with four sniffer dogs in key trade areas including control posts, airports, residences, and poacher camps with the goal of conducting over 104 seizers within a year; (2) development of a phone app to streamline data collection of trafficking incidents; and (3) maintenance of a database to record and monitor wildlife trafficking incidents to ensure that accountability exists within the local law enforcement system.</narrative>
  </description>
